THE LAST LIGHTHOUSE

FADE IN:

EXT. NORTHERN COAST - DUSK

A storm front rolls over black cliffs. Waves explode against the rocks. A lone lighthouse stands against the bruised sky.

INT. LIGHTHOUSE LAMP ROOM - NIGHT

Rain hammers the glass. MARA (60s), weathered face, silver braid, oilskin coat, trims the wick of the great lamp. Her hands are steady.

A knock echoes up the spiral stairs. Mara freezes.

MARA
Nobody comes out here in a storm.

She grabs a lantern and descends.

INT. LIGHTHOUSE ENTRANCE - CONTINUOUS

Mara pulls open the heavy door. ELI (20s), soaked, thin, a red scarf around his neck, clutches a waterproof case to his chest.

ELI
Please. The road's gone. I just need until morning.

MARA
(beat)
Then you'd better learn to keep a light burning.

EXT. NORTHERN COAST - DAWN

The storm has passed. The beam sweeps a calm, silver sea. Mara and Eli stand on the gallery, watching a fishing boat come safely home.
